From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hoechst <hoechst@trackit.systems>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 15:01:34 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] asr, meig: dial MeiG modems with +ECMDUP

On MeiG ASR modems, a context activated with +CGACT is not routed to the
RNDIS/ECM network interface: the bearer was reported connected and DHCP
worked, but no traffic passed (this went unnoticed while the modem's own
auto-dial session from power-on was still in place). +ECMDUP is the
complete dial command for the network interface: it activates the context
itself and connects it. Activating the context with +CGACT first makes the
following +ECMDUP fail.

Add an "ECM dial" option to the ASR modem and bearer, enabled by the MeiG
modem:
 - dial: +CGDCONT and *AUTHREQ as before, then
   +ECMDUP=<cid>,1,<pdp type>,<apn> instead of +CGACT
 - hang up: +ECMDUP=<cid>,0, then +CGACT=0,<cid> with errors ignored (the
   context may be the LTE default bearer, which stays active)
 - connection status: from +ECMDUP? instead of +CGACT?, since the context
   stays active when the modem drops the connection
---
